# Who answers for what ships to users and what serves them. With one account, GitHub
# never requests the owner's review (it does not ask a PR's author), and main's ruleset
# does not require it (an author cannot approve their own PR): this marks ownership, it
# does not gate merges (packaging/RELEASING.md, "GitHub settings").
# The last matching line wins, so the broad lines come first.

# The workflows, and this file.
/.github/                             @teaspoonai

# The download gate: the Worker, its deploy, and the license and data records it keeps.
/worker/                              @teaspoonai
/.github/workflows/worker-deploy.yml  @teaspoonai
/docs/engine-license-data.md          @teaspoonai

# What get.teaspoon.tech serves: the release manifests (and anything that signs or checks
# them), their publish workflow, and the packaging and runbook behind each release.
/manifest/                            @teaspoonai
/.github/workflows/publish.yml        @teaspoonai
/packaging/                           @teaspoonai

# What a box runs as root: the installer (its license acceptance included) and its bootstrap.
/install.sh                           @teaspoonai
/install-bootstrap.sh*                @teaspoonai
